  Adapted from dithercn: the 64 x 64 blue-noise threshold data
  (src/blue-noise.bin), the ordered and error-diffusion dithering techniques,
  the field-based approach to dithered surfaces, many of the example fields
  (src/fields.rs), the dithered globe (src/globe.rs) and its encoded world land
  mask (src/land.rs), and the loaders (src/loader.rs).

dither-kit
  https://tripwire.sh/dither-kit
  By ripgrim. No licence is published with the registry source.

  zkit's chart marks (src/chart.rs), generative avatars (src/avatar.rs) and the
  GPUI dithered buttons follow dither-kit's design: gradient, hatched, dotted
  and solid series fills, stacking, ribbon lines, radar charts, and symmetric
  name-derived avatars with a hue per name. These are independent Rust
  implementations; no dither-kit source code is included.

Natural Earth
  https://www.naturalearthdata.com
  The world land mask is derived from Natural Earth 1:50m land polygons, which
  are in the public domain.
